          "content": "22"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.147,
            0.525,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\frac { - b } { a } ,",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.19,
            0.514,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha \\beta + \\beta \\gamma + \\gamma \\alpha = \\frac{c}{a},",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.38,
            0.231,
            0.528,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha \\beta \\gamma = \\frac { - d } { a } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.274,
            0.372,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider an example."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.315,
            0.902,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": "Example 5\\* : Verify that $3,   -1,   -\\frac{1}{3}$ are the zeroes of the cubic polynomial $p(x)=3x^{3}-5x^{2}-11x-3$ , and then verify the relationship between the zeroes and the coefficients."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.402,
            0.82,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": "Solution : Comparing the given polynomial with $a x ^ { 3 } + b x ^ { 2 } + c x + d ,$ we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.427,
            0.537,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "$a=3,   b=-5,   c=-11,   d=-3.$ Further"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.451,
            0.732,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "p(3)=3\\times3^{3}-(5\\times3^{2})-(11\\times3)=3=81-45-33-3=0,",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.476,
            0.798,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "p(-1)=3\\times(-1)^{3}-5\\times(-1)^{2}-11\\times(-1)-3=-3=5+11-3=0,",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.505,
            0.65,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}p\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) &= 3 \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3 - 5 \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2 - 11 \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 3 \\\\&= -\\frac{1}{9} - \\frac{5}{9} + \\frac{11}{3} - 3 = -\\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} = 0\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.615,
            0.705,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $3,-1   and   -\\frac{1}{3}   are the zeros of   3x^3 - 5x^2 - 11x - 3.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.651,
            0.473,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "So, we take $\\alpha = 3, \\beta = -1   and   \\gamma = -\\frac{1}{3}.$ 1T"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.685,
            0.158,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": "Now,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.705,
            0.695,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 3 + (-1) + \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) = 2 - \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{-(-5)}{3} = \\frac{-b}{a},",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.755,
            0.891,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha \\beta + \\beta \\gamma + \\gamma \\alpha = 3 \\times (-1) + (-1) \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) + \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\times 3 = -3 + \\frac{1}{3} - 1 = -\\frac{11}{3} = \\frac{c}{a}",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.812,
            0.568,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "\\alpha \\beta \\gamma = 3 \\times (-1) \\times \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) = 1 = \\frac{-(-3)}{3} = \\frac{-d}{a} \\cdot",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_footnote",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.875,
            0.467,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "\\*Not from the examination point of view."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
